Subject: [PATCH 28/28] =?UTF-8?q?turbopack-wasi:=20the=20on-disk=20store?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20works=20now=20=E2=80=94=20reword=20the=20wasi=20persist=20ga?=
 =?UTF-8?q?te?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The store no longer trips anything on wasi (the real blocker was memmap2 having
no wasip1 backend, now fixed by the FileMap owned-buffer fallback). Correct the
stale comment (it blamed a thread-local/SyncUnsafeCell concurrency assertion
that was never the cause) and reframe the TURBOPACK_WASI_ALLOW_DISK_STORE opt-in
as a deliberate policy gate — kept off by default because the browser runtime's
store lives in OPFS and a real app's cache is ~1GB+, not because it's broken.
---
 .../src/next_api/turbopack_ctx.rs             | 25 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/next-napi-bindings/src/next_api/turbopack_ctx.rs b/crates/next-napi-bindings/src/next_api/turbopack_ctx.rs
index 26e1a32c..5c41a023 100644
--- a/crates/next-napi-bindings/src/next_api/turbopack_ctx.rs
+++ b/crates/next-napi-bindings/src/next_api/turbopack_ctx.rs
@@ -266,21 +266,24 @@ pub fn create_turbo_tasks(
     skip_compaction: bool,
     turbopack_memory_eviction: MemoryEvictionMode,
 ) -> Result<NextTurboTasks> {
-    // The on-disk turbo-persistence store currently trips write-batch
-    // concurrency assertions on wasi: its write path hands out `&mut` from a
-    // thread-local `SyncUnsafeCell`, which is only sound while thread ids are
-    // not recycled, and the wasi pthread pool (built with `on_thread_stop` plus
-    // an idle-timing-out blocking pool) churns threads mid-batch. Until that is
-    // hardened, force the in-memory (noop) backing store on wasi. Set
-    // TURBOPACK_WASI_ALLOW_DISK_STORE=1 to opt back into the on-disk path (for
-    // reproducing/bisecting the store bug).
+    // The on-disk turbo-persistence store now works on wasi (verified end-to-end
+    // at cal.com scale: write -> restore -> compaction) since the memmap2 ->
+    // owned-buffer read fallback landed — before that, every snapshot commit
+    // failed with "Failed to mmap: platform not supported" and silently rolled
+    // back, persisting nothing. It is kept OFF by default here for a different,
+    // deliberate reason: on the browser runtime the store lives in OPFS and a
+    // real app's cache is large (~1GB+ for cal.com), so we don't want every wasi
+    // build to silently fill the user's origin storage. Opt in with
+    // TURBOPACK_WASI_ALLOW_DISK_STORE=1 (host builds with disk to spare, or once
+    // an OPFS quota/eviction policy is in place). This is a policy gate, not a
+    // correctness one.
     #[cfg(target_os = "wasi")]
     let persistent_caching = {
         if persistent_caching && std::env::var_os("TURBOPACK_WASI_ALLOW_DISK_STORE").is_none() {
             tracing::warn!(
-                "persistent (on-disk) caching was requested but is not yet supported on \
-                 wasi; falling back to the in-memory store. Set \
-                 TURBOPACK_WASI_ALLOW_DISK_STORE=1 to force the on-disk path."
+                "persistent (on-disk) caching is supported on wasi but kept off by default \
+                 (browser OPFS storage footprint); using the in-memory store. Set \
+                 TURBOPACK_WASI_ALLOW_DISK_STORE=1 to enable the on-disk path."
             );
             false
         } else {
